      "content": "but it doesnt feel like a choice though. it feels like biology. like, staring at a blood test and seeing my whole future written in the cells. if the data says i'm broken, how is therapy gonna change my actual DNA? it just feels like i'm fighting a losing war against my own body. like why even bother pretending i can change something that was decided before i was even born? to what struggle against the it it just",
