      "content": "\"playing my own game\" sounds nice but it's just a way to sugarcoat it. if the script says the end of the story is tragedy, then the \"tools\" are just making the middle part longer and more painful. it feels more like just prolonging the inevitable. if it's truly just a biological function, like a machine breaking down, isn't there just a point where it's more logical to just accept it instead of fighting to stay functional when the hardware is fundamentally failed?\n volare no? in dragging it the outcome is",
